                            ║ Host shows the users, groups and folder permissions of this  ║known                      │
                            ║ machine. Admin means sudo rights, Docker is practically      ║                           │
                            ║ root, and enabled means membership of the group sysmin. Grey ║ the fields only root can  │
                            ║ rows are system accounts; space hides them. Folders reads    ║                           │
                            ║ one path at a time: type it, tab completes, enter reads. A   ║───────────────────────────╯
                            ║ path marked protected is a system path. Changes lists the    ║                            
                            ║ latest changes made through sysmin and undoes one with       ║                            
                            ║ enter. What only root can read, such as the locked state and ║                            
                            ║ SSH keys of a user or the list of changes, is read through   ║                            
                            ║ sudo when you press ctrl+r; sudo asks for the password,      ║                            
                            ║ sysmin never sees it.                                        ║                            
